Article 40
(1) Services in fulfilling the rights of women and children are implemented based on the following principles:
a. empathy;
b. confidentiality;
c. fast and responsive;
d. humanity;
e. documented;
f. inclusion;
g. impartial;
h. victim-oriented;
i. accessible and excellent;
j. professional; and
k. sustainability.
(2) The provision of services is carried out with attention to the situation and condition of the reporter, victim, and/or witness.
(3) To improve the provision of services as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government establishes community-based integrated women and child protection institutions at the Village/Sub-district level.

